{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"OESA-2026-1684","published":"2026-03-20T11:10:43Z","modified":"2026-08-18T01:19:41.757931654Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-2443"],"summary":"libsoup security update","details":"libsoup is an HTTP client/server library for GNOME. It uses GObjects and the glib main loop, to integrate well with GNOME applications, and also has a synchronous API, for use in threaded applications.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nA flaw was identified in libsoup, a widely used HTTP library in GNOME-based systems. When processing specially crafted HTTP Range headers, the library may improperly validate requested byte ranges. In certain build configurations, this could allow a remote attacker to access portions of server memory beyond the intended response. Exploitation requires a vulnerable configuration and access to a server using the embedded SoupServer component.(CVE-2026-2443)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"libsoup","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP2","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/libsoup&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP2"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2.74.3-15.oe2403sp2"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["libsoup-2.74.3-15.oe2403sp2.aarch64.rpm","libsoup-debuginfo-2.74.3-15.oe2403sp2.aarch64.rpm","libsoup-debugsource-2.74.3-15.oe2403sp2.aarch64.rpm","libsoup-devel-2.74.3-15.oe2403sp2.aarch64.rpm"],"noarch":["libsoup-help-2.74.3-15.oe2403sp2.noarch.rpm"],"src":["libsoup-2.74.3-15.oe2403sp2.src.rpm"],"x86_64":["libsoup-2.74.3-15.oe2403sp2.x86_64.rpm","libsoup-debuginfo-2.74.3-15.oe2403sp2.x86_64.rpm","libsoup-debugsource-2.74.3-15.oe2403sp2.x86_64.rpm","libsoup-devel-2.74.3-15.oe2403sp2.x86_64.rpm"]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://repo.openeuler.org/security/data/osv/OESA-2026-1684.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libsoup","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP3","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/libsoup&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP3"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2.74.3-15.oe2403sp3"}]}],"e